1
00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,117
Euchate and Thank

2
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:37,200
you.

3
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:37,937
I certainly had my hands full
looking for that elusive eighth

4
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:41,477
child and at the same time trying
to hide Tentomon from my parents.

5
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:46,217
For some unexplained reason, there was a
strange Digify signal moving all over town.

6
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:49,360
It confused everybody,
including DemiDevimon.

7
00:01:49,840 --> 00:01:54,237
Meanwhile, Kabuterimon really got a nose
fill when he went up against Raremon,

8
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:58,837
a very odorous Digimon with a body
structure unlike any I've ever seen before.

9
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,900
But ultimately, he was
no match for Kabuterimon.

10
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:07,082
Most curious, with all this excitement,
you'd think we were back in the Digi-World.

11
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:10,860
Let's go, Tokyo Tower!

12
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,940
S. Melanmon!

13
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:06,040
Oh, my God.

14
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,440
I hate this fog!

15
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:16,657
Master, where are you?

16
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,564
I'm getting mildew on my wings!

17
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,160
Aha! Finally!

18
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:25,480
Sheesh, you couldn't take
a cap like everyone else?

19
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:34,660
At last, I was starting to worry!

20
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,000
Calm down.

21
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:39,637
I went out to have a bite to eat
and to get familiar with the city.

22
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:43,857
It is always so difficult to get a
good meal when one is away from home.

23
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:44,770
Yeah, right.

24
00:03:44,853 --> 00:03:46,177
So what do we do next, boss?

25
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:48,677
We are continuing the
search for the Eighth Child.

26
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:51,080
The details are of no concern to you.

27
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:54,300
Well, as I always say,
uh, whatever you say!

28
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,200
Ah, come on.

29
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:13,068
Where did I put that thing?

30
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:16,010
Junk.

31
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:17,110
Stuff.

32
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:19,220
More junk. More stuff.

33
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,120
Man, I was a messy kid.

34
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:23,660
I can't believe how unorganized I was.

35
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,000
What you doing?

36
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,145
Looking for my old phone book.

37
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:33,077
It'll have exactly what I need.

38
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,360
And I'm helping.

39
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:37,170
How come?

40
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,128
And now, today's top story.

41
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,157
The monsters that are plaguing the city.

42
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:42,857
Still no official comment on where the

43
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,705
creatures are from or
what they might be after.

44
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:49,168
We will keep you updated
throughout the day.

45
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,091
Meanwhile, in other news,

46
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,217
health officials report
young women all over

47
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,829
the city are being
hospitalized for anemia.

48
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:56,870
Just a moment.

49
00:04:56,953 --> 00:04:58,217
No word on whether the
cases are connected.

50
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,057
But doctors are voicing
concern that so many seemingly

51
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:04,097
healthy young women are being
struck down so suddenly.

52
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,709
Tai, it's your friend Izzy.

53
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,130
Coming!

54
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,560
Hey! Hey! Ready to go?

55
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:20,337
Agumon, you digivolved.

56
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,250
You bet I did.

57
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,126
All I needed was a good meal.

58
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,250
Psst!

59
00:05:24,333 --> 00:05:25,580
It's me, Tentomon.

60
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:27,880
Nice disguise, dude. Thanks, Tai.

61
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,571
I put it together myself.

62
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,192
Wait till Mimi sees you.

63
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,221
I need one, too.

64
00:05:33,180 --> 00:05:34,010
Yeah.

65
00:05:34,093 --> 00:05:34,923
Any ideas?

66
00:05:35,006 --> 00:05:35,836
Mm-hmm.

67
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,221
Yes, I think so.

68
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,940
Hey, Charlie, over here.

69
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:40,690
Mommy.

70
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:44,340
Yeah, real inconspicuous.

71
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:50,480
So, Tai, did you find your
address book from school?

72
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:55,460
Oh, uh, well, Sora was in my class,
so I thought we'd just use hers.

73
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:56,930
Uh-huh.

74
00:05:57,013 --> 00:05:57,934
Couldn't find it, huh?

75
00:06:00,920 --> 00:06:02,437
All right, listen up, everybody.

76
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:06,780
I called you all here today because,
well, there was nothing good on TV.

77
00:06:07,380 --> 00:06:08,210
Ha-ha.

78
00:06:08,293 --> 00:06:09,123
Very funny, Tai.

79
00:06:09,206 --> 00:06:10,237
So where are the others?

80
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:11,150
Hey, wait.

81
00:06:11,233 --> 00:06:12,573
Don't start without me.

82
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,270
Good morning.

83
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:16,060
Okay, so where's Mimi?

84
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,320
She's probably out buying clothes.

85
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,137
Oh, get out and walk.

86
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,577
You're too heavy to push.

87
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:22,897
Mimi, how's that going to look?

88
00:06:22,980 --> 00:06:24,837
I'm supposed to be a little baby.

89
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,897
You just grew up.

90
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:26,810
Now get out.

91
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,820
Hey, did you guys see it?

92
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:31,757
It was all over the
news on TV this morning.

93
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:35,637
More and more of Myotismon's
Digibozos are popping up in the city.

94
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:38,140
And they're very real. What do you mean?

95
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:42,277
The last time we came back, there were
Digimon all over the place, like now.

96
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,419
But only Kari and I could see them.

97
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:49,621
Everybody else walked right by
them, as if they weren't even there.

98
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:54,597
Now even normal people see them, and
they're on the news and everything.

99
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,033
It's like they're really here this time.

100
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:00,577
Maybe it's because this time they came
through the gate that Myotismon made.

101
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:01,840
I don't like it.

102
00:07:01,980 --> 00:07:05,617
If they can be seen, then they're physically
here, and if they're here physically,

103
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,700
they can do a whole lot of damage.

104
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,001
Yeah, like what?

105
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:13,438
Do I really need to remind you what
those evil Digimon are capable of?

106
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,750
Creepy!

107
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:16,740
Complete systems failure.

108
00:07:17,140 --> 00:07:18,817
So what are we sitting around here for?

109
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:22,177
We better get out there and find that
eighth kid if we want to stop these guys.

110
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:24,517
Save the Digi-World
and we'll save our own!

111
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:27,080
Go, Tai! Uh-huh. What's the plan?

112
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,040
Well, I've got a few.

113
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,697
I want to hear Izzy's theory.

114
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:34,017
Don't start until I get there.

115
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:35,057
I love Izzy's theories.

116
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:35,970
Hold on.

117
00:07:36,053 --> 00:07:38,195
All right, we won't start without you.

118
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,857
We've already concluded that when
the Digimon attacked four years ago,

119
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:44,881
all of us, including the
Eighth Child, were there.

120
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:49,940
It is also safe to assume that each of
us were given Digivices for a reason.

121
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,797
Last night, I picked up an
unidentified Digivice reading.

122
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:55,762
I think it was the Eighth Child.

123
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:57,457
Obviously, I lost a signal,

124
00:07:57,540 --> 00:08:00,237
but it's clear that the Eighth
Child is in this vicinity.

125
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:02,417
That's why the monsters are here, too.

126
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,088
Monsters worse than snakes.

127
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,997
And this is supposed to help us? I'm lost.

128
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:10,497
My conclusion is that the Eighth Child is
somewhere in one of these address books.

129
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:11,410
Somehow,

130
00:08:11,493 --> 00:08:12,677
we have to make a lot of calls and patrol

131
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,177
the city for monster
attacks at the same time.

132
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:18,837
Well, I guess I could do some calling,
as long as my folks don't find out.

133
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,797
But I really got to do
some serious studying,

134
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,197
so I won't be able to go
on the search with you.

135
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,110
What?

136
00:08:24,193 --> 00:08:25,023
Joe, it's summer.

137
00:08:25,106 --> 00:08:29,252
I'm getting an early start This year
I'm really gonna be prepared Here then

138
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:32,917
If you're not coming with us Then you
might as well do my calling for me Okay,

139
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,100
thanks Joe,

140
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:36,317
we're talking about the fate of
the world here If you're gonna

141
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:40,077
chicken out You can call all the
names in my book too See ya Yes,

142
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,837
it might make more sense Having
one person concentrate on all the

143
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,920
phone calling Rather than split it
up He has a point there Good luck

144
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:48,750
Wait a minute

145
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:52,657
No, Tai Not yours too, please
I'm not that kind of guy,

146
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:56,057
Joe Don't worry, it's my job and
you've got enough on your plate.

147
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:59,340
Oh, man, Tai, you're a totally
great guy. Thanks a lot.

148
00:08:59,860 --> 00:09:00,800
Well, you know.

149
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,150
Mr.

150
00:09:02,233 --> 00:09:04,257
Generous, I bet he couldn't
find his address book.

151
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,928
Well, how'd you ever guess?

152
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:10,637
Whoa, look at all that damage
from last night's battle.

153
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:13,117
And there'll be a lot
more, too, if this goes on.

154
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:15,657
We've got to hurry up and
find that eighth child.

155
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:16,570
We will.

156
00:09:16,653 --> 00:09:19,225
We're not called the
Digidestined for nothing.

157
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:23,037
Master, are we almost there yet?

158
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:25,860
because all this water is making me crazy.

159
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,720
Those Digidestined brats are
probably miles away by now.

160
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:44,780
Hey, look.

161
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,577
That fog's coming in again.

162
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,497
I've never seen anything like it.

163
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:51,237
At the same time, we're having
the hottest weather on record.

164
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:54,580
And I heard that somebody
saw snow falling last night.

165
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:58,074
The ozone layer must be messed
up worse than we thought.

166
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,900
Welcome, O Great One.

167
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,040
All is ready.

168
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,240
Perfect, Gatomar.

169
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,933
As always, you have done excellent work.

170
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:19,257
Hey, Whiskers, what do
you think you're doing?

171
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:21,640
I don't think I know why I'm here.

172
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,377
I'm finding the eighth child.

173
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:24,960
That's my job, furball.

174
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,300
I'm in charge here. Yeah, right.

175
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,677
Listen up, puss in boots.

176
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,525
Quit sucking up to the master.

177
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,621
I'm the master's cute little pet.

178
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:35,034
Get me with a furball.

179
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:39,117
It's really hard to feel threatened
by a bowling ball with feathers.

180
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,517
Just keep out of my way.

181
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,365
I'm finding that kid, not you.

182
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:43,370
Got it?

183
00:10:43,453 --> 00:10:45,440
Take a catnap, kitty litter.

184
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:51,798
That flappy-winged Joker couldn't
find water if he fell out of a boat.

185
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,997
Okay, so we'll split up into pairs
so we can cover more of the city.

186
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,940
Got it? Got it. Let's
go. Good luck, everybody.

187
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:22,120
I see food.

188
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:25,028
Agumon, keep your mind
on our mission, okay?

189
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,070
Anything?

190
00:11:28,153 --> 00:11:29,118
You can't catch me.

191
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,800
Come on.

192
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,300
Yeah, you got it, Mom.

193
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,740
No, there's nothing yet.

194
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:41,060
Aw, it doesn't look like he's down here.

195
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:44,940
That would have been too
easy anyway. Yeah, right.

196
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:49,450
Hi.

197
00:11:49,533 --> 00:11:52,977
I know this is kind of strange,
but I was in second grade with you.

198
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:54,200
Hey, stop pushing.

199
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,437
I am not pushing you.

200
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:56,577
You're kicking me.

201
00:11:56,660 --> 00:11:59,117
You crossed the line onto
my side, you big cheater.

202
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,277
I am not a cheater.

203
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:01,190
You're a liar.

204
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:02,510
I'm telling...

205
00:12:02,593 --> 00:12:03,423
Knock it off.

206
00:12:03,506 --> 00:12:05,557
If you two keep fooling around,
someone's going to get hurt.

207
00:12:05,640 --> 00:12:06,875
I know how they feel.

208
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:10,984
Just walking around in this heat's
enough to make anybody cranky.

209
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:12,747
You know what this is, Sora?

210
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:14,160
A big fat drag.

211
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,600
What silly creatures.

212
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:22,500
Pea-brained dolts, laugh it up.

213
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:25,621
When my Myotismon is through,
you won't be laughing.

214
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,577
Miko, come back here.

215
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:28,542
Where'd you go?

216
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:29,990
Miko!

217
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,960
What a funny-looking kitty.

218
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,520
Hi there.

219
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,937
Are you a friend of Agumon?

220
00:12:43,020 --> 00:12:43,850
Huh?

221
00:12:43,933 --> 00:12:45,040
Are you one of them?

222
00:12:47,860 --> 00:12:48,860
What's your name?

223
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:53,260
Wait, don't go.

224
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:01,240
So, she knows about Agumon.

225
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:05,676
Is it possible this little
squirt is the eighth child?

226
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,400
Hey, I know you're there.

227
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,440
You can come in if you
want to. Mom's not home.

228
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:30,160
Weather experts can't explain
the unseasonable fog. In fact,

229
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:31,897
they have no explanation for any of the

230
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,777
bizarre weather conditions
we've been having,

231
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:35,331
including this heat wave.

232
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,557
I'm not meant for this kind of work.

233
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,080
If I ever have a baby,

234
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:43,006
I'm going to hire somebody to
push her around, that's for sure.

235
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:43,950
Hold on.

236
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,532
How about a break, okay?

237
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,070
Again?

238
00:13:47,153 --> 00:13:48,096
We'll make it quick.

239
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:53,537
Last night, I got to sleep
in a soft bed with the A .C.

240
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:55,500
cranked up, watching my own TV.

241
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,077
Wasn't that the best, Belmont?

242
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,977
Dinner was really something, too.

243
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:00,001
Wasn't it great?

244
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:03,217
My mom knows all the best
take-out places in the city.

245
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,557
She never has to cook.

246
00:14:04,640 --> 00:14:07,277
Zara's mom made our dinner,
and it was terrific.

247
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:10,517
Well, all of it except for this
kind of green, mushy stuff.

248
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,600
What's it called?

249
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:12,910
What?

250
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:14,770
Spinach.

251
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,320
Now, let's see. Where was I?

252
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:20,090
Hmm.

253
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,817
Would you look at that?

254
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,135
She's not even tired.

255
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,150
You're different.

256
00:14:25,233 --> 00:14:26,866
You like to take things easy.

257
00:14:27,340 --> 00:14:30,340
Finding this kid's harder
than finding a good sail.

258
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,577
Hey, Sora, if we really
want to find this kid,

259
